igures sourced from the chargeback reporting capability\n  delivered by this strategy (the reporting backend with its retrieval surface)\n  — the Dashboard must not re-implement report computation or metering\n  collection.\n- Quota figures reflecting each project's Kueue quota as configured in the\n  platform (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, read via the Dashboard's\n  existing Kubernetes-API-based integration pattern).\n- Placement in the Dashboard's administrator-facing area, consistent with\n  existing Dashboard integration patterns (navigation, resource views).\n\nOut of scope: the report computation, CSV export, and retrieval API (owned by\nthe Distributed Workloads team); the metering collection pipeline\n(RHAISTRAT-9990).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The Dashboard presents, in its administrator-facing area, a view listing\n  projects with their current-month GPU-hour consumption shown against their\n  Kueue quota.\n- For a project with known metered usage and a configured quota, the view\n  displays the consumption and quota figures that match the reporting backend's\n  computed values for the current month.\n- The consumption data displayed is traceable to the chargeback reporting\n  capability (no report computation or metering collection implemented in the\n  Dashboard) — verified by code review.\n- The view renders for administrators of the platform and follows the\n  Dashboard's established integration patterns.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|---|---|---|\n| HLR-3 | P1 | The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota. |\n--- artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E003-ai-signals.md\n# AI Implementability Signals — RHAISTRAT-9018-E003\n\nChargeback reporting documentation: report semantics and export integration\n(Implementation, docs-authoring, RHOAI Documentation).\n\n| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| change_specificity | 1 | HLR-4 enumerates the doc topics concr