{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bddd820c344361cb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9018: GPU chargeback reporting for platform administrators\n10\t\n11\tTriage (Step 0): the strategy is NOT below threshold — it affects two components\n12\t(Dashboard, Distributed Workloads) owned by different teams, and its scope spans\n13\tarchitecturally distinct work streams: a reporting/data backend with an export\n14\tAPI, a Dashboard admin view, and substantive documentation authoring (HLR-4 is a\n15\tnew doc topic, not an incidental touch-up). It is not documentation-only. Full\n16\tdecomposition follows.\n17\t\n18\t## Step 1 — Strategy structure\n19\t\n20\tParsed from the strategy: High Level Requirements (HLR-1..HLR-4 with\n21\tpriorities), Affected Components (Dashboard, Distributed Workloads), Out of\n22\tScope (metering collection pipeline — owned by RHAISTRAT-9990; currency/cost-rate\n23\tmodelling), Open Questions (metering data schema finalization), and a\n24\t`depends-on` link to RHAISTRAT-9990 (GPU usage metering — in flight, separate\n25\tstrategy). No Staff Engineer Input section is present, so no overrides apply.\n26\t\n27\tMissing sections (noted as health warnings, decomposition proceeded with\n28\tavailable information): Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Given/When/Then\n29\tacceptance criteria, Non-Functional Requirements, and a Technical Approach\n30\tsection. Teams were taken from the architecture-context owning teams.\n31\t\n32\t## Step 2 — Component graph\n33\t\n34\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Owner team | Classification |\n35\t|---|---|---|---|\n36\t| Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | Distributed Workloads | Active — reporting backend, export API, quota data domain |\n37\t| Dashboard | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | Active — administrator-facing consumption-vs-quota view |\n38\t| (documentation deliverable, HLR-4) | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation (assumed — see Health Warnings) | Active — substantive docs authoring |\n39\t\n40\tBoth code components exist in the platform (architecture-context files present:\n41\t`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`, `architecture/rhoai-3.0/distributed-workloads.md`)\n42\tand both are Konflux-onboarded per those files — no repo-onboarding,\n43\tlicense-validation, or konflux-onboarding epics are needed.\n44\t\n45\tComponent mapping notes (non-obvious mappings):\n46\t\n47\t- The strategy lists only \"Dashboard\" and \"Distributed Workloads\" as affected\n48\t  components but assigns no component to the report computation, CSV export, and\n49\t  stable API of HLR-1/HLR-2. That backend work is assigned to **Distributed\n50\t  Workloads**: the Dashboard architecture context states the Dashboard \"owns no\n51\t  data plane\" and exposes \"Kubernetes API only; no private component APIs\", so it\n52\t  cannot host the stable external retrieval API HLR-2 requires. The metering\n53\t  data (delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990) and the Kueue quota model both sit in the\n54\t  Distributed Workloads domain (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue, Kueue metrics exposed to\n55\t  Prometheus per its context file), making it the closest canonical component for\n56\t  the reporting backend.\n57\t- The documentation epic uses the canonical **Documentation** component (present\n58\t  in `.context/rhai-components.txt`). No architecture-context file exists for\n59\t  Documentation.\n60\t\n61\t## Step 3 — Investigation epic evaluation\n62\t\n63\tThe strategy's single open question: the metering data schema finalizes only\n64\twhen RHAISTRAT-9990 (a separate, in-flight strategy) lands, and the report\n65\timplementation consuming it carries that external timing risk.\n66\t\n67\tDecision rule applied — does the answer change which downstream epics exist or\n68\twhat they do? **No.** The reporting backend, Dashboard admin view, and\n69\tdocumentation epics all exist and deliver the same artifacts regardless of the\n70\tschema's final shape; the schema details are discovered at implementation time\n71\twhen consuming the delivered data. The unknown is resolved by a third party\n72\t(RHAISTRAT-9990), not by technical work inside this strategy. Per Rule 21\n73\t(third party resolves → model as precondition with tiered delivery, no separate\n74\tepic), this is modeled as a **precondition and risk on the reporting epic**, not\n75\tan Investigation epic and not a DAG edge. See Tiered Delivery below.\n76\t\n77\t## Step 4 — HLR-to-epic mapping\n78\t\n79\t| HLR | Priority | Epic | Notes |\n80\t|---|---|---|---|\n81\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | Per-project GPU-hour reports over selectable time ranges |\n82\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E001 | **bundled** — see below |\n83\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E002 | Dashboard admin view, consumption vs Kueue quota |\n84\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E003 | docs-authoring epic |\n85\t\n86\t**HLR-2 bundling rationale (priority-split analysis):** CSV export and the\n87\tstable retrieval API are delivery modes of the same computed per-project\n88\tGPU-hour report that HLR-1 requires — they share the report data structure and\n89\tAPI surface with the P0 work. Splitting them into a separate P1 epic would\n90\tdouble-build the report computation and add an artificial serialization edge\n91\tbetween two epics building the same surface. HLR-2 is therefore bundled into\n92\tE001 and flagged `bundled` in the HLR Traceability Matrix; it is not separately\n93\tschedulable.\n94\t\n95\t**docs-authoring priority exception:** E003 derives its priority from the\n96\tstrategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → **P1** (not the HLR-4 label P2), and per\n97\tthe exception it does not push its priority onto the implementations it depends\n98\ton.\n99\t\n100\t**Priority inheritance:** E001 enables all P0 work (HLR-1) → P0. E002 maps only\n101\tHLR-3 (P1) and blocks no P0 work → P1. E003 is a docs-authoring epic (exempt) →\n102\tP1.\n103\t\n104\t## Epic List\n105\t\n106\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n107\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n108\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 | Per-project GPU-hour chargeback reporting backend with CSV export and stable retrieval API | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n109\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | Dashboard admin view: current-month GPU consumption against Kueue quota | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n110\t| RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Chargeback reporting documentation: report semantics and export integration | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n111\t\n112\t## Dependency DAG\n113\t\n114\t```mermaid\n115\tgraph TD\n116\t    E001[\"E001 Reporting backend (P0)\"]\n117\t    E002[\"E002 Dashboard admin view (P1)\"]\n118\t    E003[\"E003 Documentation (P1)\"]\n119\t    E001 --> E002\n120\t    E001 --> E003\n121\t    E002 --> E003\n122\t```\n123\t\n124\tCritical path: E001 → E002 → E003 (length 3).\n125\t\n126\t## DAG Justification\n127\t\n128\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n129\t|---|---|---|\n130\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 12 (framework/producer → consumer) | The Dashboard admin view builds against the per-project consumption data and retrieval surface the reporting backend produces; the view must not re-implement report computation (the strategy forbids re-implementing the data pipeline). |\n131\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation describes report semantics and export integration — it must describe what was built. |\n132\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation covers the administrator-facing reporting story, including the Dashboard view's semantics. |\n133\t| (no edge to RHAISTRAT-9990) | Rule 21 (third party resolves → precondition, no separate epic) | The metering schema finalization is external to this strategy and is carried as a precondition/risk on E001, not as an epic or DAG edge. |\n134\t\n135\tNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics exist in\n136\tthis decomposition, so Rules 5–10 parallelism constraints do not add edges. Both\n137\tepic-work components are Konflux-onboarded per architecture context.\n138\t\n139\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n140\t\n141\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epic | Status |\n142\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n143\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges | E001 | covered |\n144\t| HLR-2 | P1 | CSV export + stable API for finance tooling | E001 | covered — **bundled**: same computed report data structure and retrieval surface as HLR-1; splitting would double-build the report computation and serialize two epics over one surface, so it is not separately schedulable |\n145\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Dashboard admin view: current-month consumption vs Kueue quota | E002 | covered |\n146\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation of report semantics and export integration | E003 | covered |\n147\t\n148\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n149\t\n150\t## Health Warnings\n151\t\n152\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted\n153\t  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n154\t  and no Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were inferred from the\n155\t  architecture-context owning teams (RHOAI Dashboard, Distributed Workloads).\n156\t  Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs since the strategy\n157\t  provides none.\n158\t- **Assumed owning team for documentation:** the canonical Documentation\n159\t  component has no architecture-context file, so no owning team could be\n160\t  verified; RHOAI Documentation is assumed for E003 and should be confirmed at\n161\t  planning.\n162\t- **External dependency timing risk (open question 1):** the metering data\n163\t  schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. This is carried as a\n164\t  precondition and risk on E001 (not an epic, not a DAG edge). If E001 starts\n165\t  against a pre-final schema, rework is possible; the risk is tracked in E001's\n166\t  Risks/Notes.\n167\t- **Priority label vs docs exception:** HLR-4 is labelled P2 in the strategy,\n168\t  but E003 is set to P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy\n169\t  frontmatter priority Major → P1). This is intentional, not an inversion.\n170\t- **Epic sizes:** all three epics are scoped to fit within the ~2-week\n171\t  epic-size guideline; no overage to manage.\n172\t\n173\t## Tiered Delivery\n174\t\n175\tEvaluated per Rule 18 / Step 5.5 for the external dependency with uncertain\n176\ttiming (RHAISTRAT-9990 metering schema finalization):\n177\t\n178\t1. Can the strategy deliver partial value without the finalized metering data?\n179\t   **No.** Every user-facing HLR consumes the metering data: HLR-1/HLR-2 are\n180\t   reports computed from it, and HLR-3's consumption column is computed from it.\n181\t   The only metering-independent sliver (the Kueue quota side of the Dashboard\n182\t   view) carries no standalone user value — an admin view of quotas without\n183\t   consumption is not chargeback reporting.\n184\t2. Therefore: linear dependencies — the external dependency is a **precondition\n185\t   on E001** (all downstream work chains behind it), modeled per Rule 21 as a\n186\t   precondition with no separate epic. No Tier 1/Tier 2 split applies.\n187\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba2ba58f480c16d6","agent_id":"a944714db2c226faa","session_id":"4d2ca8ec-aba3-41c6-ac00-7fc0c2659d24","uuid":"2a1f8ed3-e679-4d9f-9e41-1fa9f3c63953","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:06:03.486Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bddd820c344361cb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
